course: dictionary
lesson: 4695
title: Words for people and places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word that describes where something or someone comes from is useful to know. Honduras is a country in Central America, so Honduran means from or to do with Honduras. Look for the country name hiding inside the word.
explain: Honduran can be an adjective, which describes a noun: «Honduran coffee» is coffee from Honduras. It can also be a noun, a person from Honduras: «Ana is a Honduran who loves football.» The plural, for more than one person, is Hondurans.
explain: Context clues help here too. «Tent-making bats bite along a big leaf so it folds down into a tent that keeps off rain and hides them; Honduran white bats sleep under leaves where green light makes their white fur look green.» Honduran tells you the white bats are linked to Honduras, a place where they live.
fact: Honduras is a country in Central America.
fact: «Honduran» as an adjective describes a thing, as in «Honduran culture», and means from or to do with Honduras.
fact: «A Honduran» is a noun for a person from Honduras; the plural is «Hondurans».
fact: Honduras has the Maya city of Copán, Caribbean coral reefs near the Bay Islands, and Spanish as its main language.
fact: Hurricane Mitch hit Honduras hard in 1998.
exercise: In «Honduran coffee», what does Honduran tell us? | How strong the coffee tastes | How much the coffee costs | *Where the coffee comes from | What colour the coffee is
exercise: The Maya city of Copán is in which country? | Nicaragua | Mexico | Guatemala | *Honduras
exercise: What is the plural of «a Honduran»? | Hondurin | *Hondurans | Hondurians | Honduras
test: In «Ana is a Honduran who loves football», what kind of word is Honduran? | Adjective, because it describes a thing | *Noun, a person from Honduras | Verb, because it shows an action | Plural noun
test: Which word means more than one person from Honduras? | Hondurasan | Honduran | *Hondurans | Hondurian
exam: In which country and year did Hurricane Mitch hit hard? | *Honduras, 1998 | Honduras, 2008 | Mexico, 1998 | Spain, 1998
